bolo's own source code contains no third-party source code, except the copy
of uccharan in ui/src/vendor/uccharan (see "Web console: speech synthesis in
the browser" below), the parts of Kyutai's moshi named under "Full-duplex
speech models", and dizione in server/src/bolo/vendor/dizione: English text to
phonemes, Copyright Muhammed Nazeem, Apache License 2.0 (its LICENSE is next to
it), unchanged from https://github.com/n4ze3m/dizione at commit
8cd889e4de7be6bd1dd2e6891344a0729fa14dd4, used by the tiny-voca voice, and its
TypeScript port in ui/src/lib/browser-tts/dizione (a derivative work of that
copy, same copyright and licence; the browser demo's tiny-voca voice reads its
tables from server/src/bolo/vendor/dizione/data). It talks to the
following components, which are installed separately as Python dependencies
or optional extras and keep their own licences:

